WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.565
A client pays your team.

00:00:01.565 --> 00:00:04.068
Who gets repaid first, and who gets what?

00:00:04.068 --> 00:00:09.076
TeamPay makes that agreement clear, then handles the split in USDC on Arc.

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:12.570
Here, Ada covered sixty dollars in hosting.

00:00:12.570 --> 00:00:15.507
A small payment repays part of that cost.

00:00:15.507 --> 00:00:18.811
With three hundred dollars, her expense is repaid first.

00:00:18.811 --> 00:00:21.381
The rest follows the team's agreed shares.

00:00:22.250 --> 00:00:26.624
Create one agreement with your teammates, wallet addresses, expenses, and percentages.

00:00:26.624 --> 00:00:29.806
Preview where the money will go before publishing.

00:00:29.806 --> 00:00:32.987
Then share one payment link with your client.

00:00:33.875 --> 00:00:37.466
This is a completed mainnet test with two builder controlled wallets.

00:00:37.466 --> 00:00:41.384
Four payments totaled 0.006 USDC.

00:00:41.384 --> 00:00:44.322
The expense was repaid, and the rest split equally.

00:00:45.125 --> 00:00:49.969
Each payment has a readable receipt, showing the recipients, amounts, and transaction link.

00:00:49.969 --> 00:00:52.204
Both teammates have withdrawn their earnings.

00:00:52.204 --> 00:00:56.303
Arc uses USDC for payments and network fees.

00:00:57.125 --> 00:00:57.550
TeamPay.

00:00:57.550 --> 00:01:01.374
One client payment, expenses repaid, and clear team shares.

00:01:01.374 --> 00:01:07.748
Try the example without a wallet, inspect the verified payment, or create your team's agreement.
